     "type": "intro",
     "title": "What If You Built the Audience BEFORE the Product?",
     "content": "In 2007, a guy named **Joe Pulizzi** was a magazine executive who quit his stable job, mortgaged his house, and started blogging about a topic almost nobody cared about: 'content marketing.' He had no product. No service. No clients. Just a blog and a free newsletter.\n\nSix years later, he sold his company — the **Content Marketing Institute** — for tens of millions of dollars. He never raised venture capital. He never built a product first. He built an **audience first**, then asked them what they needed.\n\nThis is the **Content Inc. Model**, and it's the exact reverse of how the business world teaches you to start a company. By the end of this seminar, you'll know how to do it yourself.",
