     "explanation": "Pulizzi is firm: a clear category leader has accumulated SEO authority, audience trust, and brand recognition that you cannot beat by trying harder. The right move is to **tilt further** — find a narrower audience cut, a different format, a contrarian POV, or a new story angle they don't occupy. Competing head-on usually means years of work for invisible results. Trying to outwork an established leader is the Content Inc. version of trying to compete with Amazon on shipping speed.",
