     "explanation": "The six steps are sequential for a reason. In month two there is no sweet spot proven, no tilt validated, no base of consistent content, and no harvested email list — so there's no one to sell the membership TO. Worse, subscriptions are a **late-stage** stream in Pulizzi's monetization sequence (~100K+ subscribers) precisely because recurring revenue only works when a small conversion percentage still yields meaningful numbers. Validation in month two should come from audience growth signals (subscribers, replies, shares), not from premature selling. Ads are even later in the sequence, so option four is doubly wrong.",
