     "explanation": "The factors apply in order. Factor 1: her audience gathers on visual social platforms. Factor 2: a 'does this hack actually work' tilt is inherently demonstrative — viewers need to SEE the test, exactly like Ann Reardon's debunking videos. Both point decisively to video. Factor 3 (sustainability) is real — so the right answer is to design a sustainable video workflow (simpler production, batch filming), not to abandon the format the tilt demands. Personal preference is the weakest input. And 'all platforms at once' violates Step 3's core rule: one channel until it's won.",
