     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: Draw Your Monetization Map",
     "content": "Spend **30 minutes** building the revenue half of your capstone plan. You'll map Pulizzi's eight streams onto YOUR niche at each milestone.\n\n**Step 1 — Score the eight streams for fit (10 min).** For your specific niche and audience, rate each stream 1-5 on plausibility: advertising/sponsorship, events, premium content/subscriptions, books, licensing, speaking, products, consulting/services. A B2B compliance niche scores consulting high and merch low; a hobbyist baking niche reverses that.\n\n**Step 2 — Assign streams to milestones (10 min).** Build a table with rows for 1K / 10K / 25K / 50K / 100K subscribers. Place your top-scoring streams at the milestone where each becomes viable, following the high-margin-first rule. Every milestone from 10K up should have at least one named, concrete offer — not 'a course' but 'a 6-week live cohort on passing the CPC exam, $1,200.'\n\n**Step 3 — Project the first real number (5 min).** For your Milestone 1 offer: price × (1-2% of milestone audience) = projected first-launch revenue. Write it down. Is it worth the effort? If not, raise the price or change the offer — don't lower the milestone.\n\n**Step 4 — Write your trust guardrails (5 min).** Three commitments, in writing: what you will NEVER sell or endorse; your value-to-sales ratio (default 6:1); and your disclosure policy. These guardrails are the difference between a 10-year audience and a 2-year squeeze.\n\nDeliverable: a one-page map — scored streams, milestone table with named offers, one revenue projection, three guardrails.",
