     "type": "intro",
     "title": "The Furrow, the Tire Guide, and the Ad-Free Idea",
     "content": "The Content Inc. model feels like an internet-era invention — blogs, email lists, YouTube channels. But the framework is really built on businesses that predate the internet by a century. In 1895, a tractor manufacturer started mailing farmers a magazine that taught them how to farm better, barely mentioning its own equipment. In 1900, a tire company gave away a guidebook meant to get people to drive their cars into the ground faster, wearing out more tires. In 1979, a scrappy cable channel filled dead airtime with a genre nobody thought had commercial value: sports highlights and analysis, all day, every day.\n\nEach of these companies made a bet that looks backwards on paper — give away something valuable, unconnected to any single sale, for years, and the audience you build will outlast any one product cycle. That bet worked so completely that two of them are still running more than a century later.\n\nThis lesson pulls apart four of the most-cited case studies in content marketing history to find the one pattern connecting a farm-equipment maker, a French tire company, a healthcare giant, and a sports network. Name the pattern, and you can apply it to whatever niche you're building in — no tractor required.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n<text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">A CENTURY OF CONTENT INC.</text>\n<text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">Four case studies, one repeating pattern</text>\n<rect x=\"100\" y=\"170\" width=\"900\" height=\"140\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"170\" y=\"225\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">1895</text>\n<text x=\"260\" y=\"220\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\">John Deere launches The Furrow</text>\n<text x=\"260\" y=\"255\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Farming advice, barely mentions tractors</text>\n<rect x=\"100\" y=\"330\" width=\"900\" height=\"140\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"170\" y=\"385\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">1900</text>\n<text x=\"260\" y=\"380\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\">Michelin gives away its road guide</text>\n<text x=\"260\" y=\"415\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Goal: wear out tires faster</text>\n<rect x=\"100\" y=\"490\" width=\"900\" height=\"140\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"170\" y=\"545\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">Early 1900s</text>\n<text x=\"260\" y=\"540\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\">Johnson &amp; Johnson publishes safety guides</text>\n<text x=\"260\" y=\"575\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">First-aid education, not product pitches</text>\n<rect x=\"100\" y=\"650\" width=\"900\" height=\"140\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"170\" y=\"705\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">1979</text>\n<text x=\"260\" y=\"700\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"20\">ESPN signs on, fills 24 hours with content</text>\n<text x=\"260\" y=\"735\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Becomes bigger than any single game</text>\n<rect x=\"100\" y=\"820\" width=\"900\" height=\"110\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"550\" y=\"880\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"20\">Same pattern, four industries, over 125 years</text>\n</svg>",
      "caption": "The founding case studies of content marketing"
     }
